\quad - (abc + abd + abe + acd + ace + ade + bcd + bce + bde + cde)x \\
\quad + abcd + abce + abde + acde + bcde.
\end{align*}
Notice that $a, b, c, d,$ and $e$ are the roots of $f(x),$ implying that by Vieta's formula,
\begin{align*}
a + b + c + d + e &= 0, \\
ab + ac + ad + ae + bc + bd + be + cd + ce + de &= 0, \\
